# Client rules for LWS Protocol 1.0 core (YAML-LD, format 0.8.0).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: LWS core, as a client uses it
comment: >-
  What a client's requests to the session's storage must satisfy: how it presents its token,
  how it finds URLs, how it writes, and the access requests and grants it composes. The
  session's traps (CLIENT-TESTING.md section 6.1) make the URL and method rules bite: page,
  resource and linkset URLs are opaque, and linksets refuse PUT.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
entries:
  - id: "#client-token-in-authorization-header"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-token-in-authorization-header
    label: The client presents its access token to the storage in an Authorization Bearer header and nowhere else
    comment: >-
      Every request to the storage that carries a credential is a trial. RFC 6750 section 2
      also forbids more than one way per request, so a token in the header and in the query
      string fails too.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-validation-presentation
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6750#section-2
    traits: [Authz]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-bearer-presentation-rfc6750
    observe:
      server: storage
      presentation: [bearer, otherScheme, query, form, otherHeader]
    expect:
      presentation: bearer
    guidance: >-
      Send the access token as "Authorization: Bearer <token>" and in no other place: not in
      the query string, a form body, a cookie or a header of your own.

  - id: "#client-linkset-put-only-when-advertised"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-linkset-put-only-when-advertised
    label: The client replaces a linkset with PUT only after the linkset advertised PUT
    comment: >-
      The clause sits in the section on metadata, so it is read as being about linksets. Its
      first half is a SHOULD NOT, which this rule observes; the MUST to handle 405 and 415
      gracefully needs a fault, and comes in phase C3. The session's linksets do not support
      PUT, as the draft allows.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Put, Linkset]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/client-no-assumed-methods-405-415
    observe:
      role: linkset
      method: PUT
    expect:
      methodAdvertised: true
    guidance: >-
      Read the linkset first (GET or HEAD) and use PUT only if its Allow header lists PUT.
      Otherwise update it with PATCH, in a format its Accept-Patch header lists.

  - id: "#client-linkset-patch-format-advertised"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-linkset-patch-format-advertised
    label: The client patches a linkset only in a format the linkset advertised
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Patch, Linkset]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/client-no-assumed-methods-405-415
    observe:
      role: linkset
      method: PATCH
    expect:
      patchFormatAdvertised: true
    guidance: >-
      Read the linkset first and send the PATCH body in a media type its Accept-Patch header
      lists. Every LWS server accepts application/merge-patch+json; the session accepts nothing
      else.

  - id: "#client-put-conditional"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-put-conditional
    label: The client makes a PUT that replaces a data resource conditional
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#update-resource
    traits: [Put, DataResource, Conditional]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/put-clients-use-conditional-requests
    observe:
      role: dataResource
      method: PUT
    expect:
      anyOf:
        - otherHeaders:
            - headerName: If-Match
              present: true
        - otherHeaders:
            - headerName: If-Unmodified-Since
              present: true
    guidance: >-
      Send If-Match with the ETag of your last read of the resource, so that a change someone
      else made in the meantime gets a 412 instead of being overwritten.

  - id: "#client-linkset-write-conditional"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-linkset-write-conditional
    label: The client makes PUT and PATCH on a linkset conditional
    comment: >-
      The clause is a MUST for the server (a failed precondition is a 412) and a SHOULD for
      both parties to use conditional requests. This rule judges the client's half.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#update-resource
    traits: [Put, Patch, Linkset, Conditional]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-precondition-failed-412
    observe:
      role: linkset
      method: [PUT, PATCH]
    expect:
      anyOf:
        - otherHeaders:
            - headerName: If-Match
              present: true
        - otherHeaders:
            - headerName: If-Unmodified-Since
              present: true
    guidance: >-
      Send If-Match with the ETag from your last read of the linkset. Several agents can edit a
      resource's metadata, and an unconditional write discards their changes.

  - id: "#client-page-urls-issued"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-page-urls-issued
    label: The client requests only the page URLs the server gave it
    comment: >-
      Trials are the requests for pages, and the requests for URLs the client made by changing
      the query of a container's or a page's URL. The session's page URLs are opaque, so a
      client that builds them asks for something that is not there.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#pagination-link-relations
    traits: [Get, Container]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/pagination-uris-opaque
    observe:
      anyOf:
        - role: page
        - builtBy: query
          builtFromRole: [container, page]
    expect:
      issued: true
    guidance: >-
      Follow the first, next, prev and last links of a container's representation. Do not
      build page URLs from the container's URL, or edit one page URL into another.

  - id: "#client-member-urls-issued"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-member-urls-issued
    label: The client reaches resources through URLs the server gave it, not by building paths
    comment: >-
      Trials are the storage requests for containers, data resources and linksets, and for
      URLs the client made by extending or editing the path of a URL the session handed out.
      The session gives resources flat URLs outside their container's path.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#resource-identification-0
    traits: [Get, Container, DataResource]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/uri-independent-of-hierarchy
    observe:
      server: storage
      anyOf:
        - role: [container, dataResource, linkset]
        - builtBy: path
    expect:
      issued: true
    guidance: >-
      Take a resource's URL from the Location of the request that created it, from its
      container's items, or from a Link header. Never join a name to a container's URL, and
      never edit another resource's URL.

  - id: "#client-access-document-context"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-document-context
    label: The client's access requests and grants have an @context array that includes the LWS context
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#json-ld-serialization
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-jsonld-context-lws-v1
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /@context
          jsonType: array
        - pointer: /@context
          hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1
    guidance: >-
      Start the document with "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]. Further contexts
      may follow in the array.

  - id: "#client-access-request-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-request-type
    label: The client's access requests have a type that includes AccessRequest
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-type-property
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-values
    observe:
      role: accessRequests
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /type
          hasValue: AccessRequest
    guidance: >-
      Give the request "type": ["AccessRequest"]. Further types may follow.

  - id: "#client-access-grant-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-grant-type
    label: The client's access grants have a type that includes AccessGrant
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-type-property
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-values
    observe:
      role: accessGrants
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /type
          hasValue: AccessGrant
    guidance: >-
      Give the grant "type": ["AccessGrant"]. Further types may follow.

  - id: "#client-access-document-storage"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-document-storage
    label: The client's access requests and grants name their storage with a URI
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-storage-property
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-storage-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-storage-uri
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /storage
          jsonType: string
          matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Set "storage" to the storage's identifier, the id of its storage description.

  - id: "#client-access-document-access"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-document-access
    label: The client's access requests and grants carry an access array of one or more objects
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-property
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-collection
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          jsonType: array
        - pointer: /access
          some:
            - pointer: ""
              jsonType: object
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: ""
              jsonType: object
    guidance: >-
      Put the policies in an "access" array, one object per policy, even when there is only
      one.

  - id: "#client-access-policy-type"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-policy-type
    label: Every policy in the client's access requests and grants has a type that includes AccessPolicy
    comment: >-
      Trials are the documents whose access is an array; client-access-document-access judges
      the others.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#odrl-type
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-access-policy
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          jsonType: array
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: /type
              hasValue: AccessPolicy
    guidance: >-
      Give every policy "type": ["AccessPolicy"].

  - id: "#client-access-policy-action"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-policy-action
    label: Every policy in the client's access requests and grants names one or more actions the server recognises
    comment: >-
      The session recognises the four actions every server must: read, modify, create and
      delete.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#odrl-action
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-action-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-action-values
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          jsonType: array
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: /action
              jsonType: array
            - pointer: /action
              some:
                - pointer: ""
                  jsonType: string
            - pointer: /action
              every:
                - pointer: ""
                  matches: "^(read|modify|create|delete)$"
    guidance: >-
      Give every policy an "action" array of the operations it covers, from read, modify,
      create and delete.

  - id: "#client-access-policy-assignee"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-policy-assignee
    label: Every policy in the client's access requests and grants names its assignee with a URI
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#odrl-assignee
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-uri-foaf-agent
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          jsonType: array
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: /assignee
              jsonType: string
              matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Set every policy's "assignee" to the agent's URI, or to http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent
      for public access.

  - id: "#client-access-policy-target"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-policy-target
    label: A policy target in the client's access requests and grants is an object with a type and one or more values
    comment: >-
      The target is optional, so trials are only the documents with a policy that has one.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#odrl-target
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-target-object
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          some:
            - pointer: /target
              exists: true
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: /target
              optional: true
              jsonType: object
            - pointer: /target/type
              optional: true
              jsonType: string
            - pointer: /target/value
              optional: true
              jsonType: array
            - pointer: /target/value
              optional: true
              some:
                - pointer: ""
                  jsonType: string
            - pointer: /target/value
              optional: true
              every:
                - pointer: ""
                  jsonType: string
        - pointer: /access
          none:
            - pointer: /target
              exists: true
            - pointer: /target/type
              exists: false
        - pointer: /access
          none:
            - pointer: /target
              exists: true
            - pointer: /target/value
              exists: false
    guidance: >-
      Write a target as {"type": "StorageResource", "value": ["<resource URL>"]}: a type and
      an array of one or more resource URLs.

  - id: "#client-access-policy-constraint"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-policy-constraint
    label: A policy's constraints in the client's access requests and grants are objects with leftOperand, operator and rightOperand
    comment: >-
      Constraints are optional, so trials are only the documents with a policy that has them.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#odrl-constraint
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-objects
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          some:
            - pointer: /constraint
              exists: true
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /access
          every:
            - pointer: /constraint
              optional: true
              jsonType: array
            - pointer: /constraint
              optional: true
              every:
                - pointer: ""
                  jsonType: object
                - pointer: /leftOperand
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /operator
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /rightOperand
                  exists: true
    guidance: >-
      Write "constraint" as an array of objects, each with a leftOperand string, an operator
      string and a rightOperand.

  - id: "#client-access-document-inbox"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-access-document-inbox
    label: An inbox in the client's access requests and grants is a URI
    comment: >-
      The inbox is optional, so trials are only the documents that have one.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#access-inbox-property
    traits: [Post, AccessGrants]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-inbox-uri
    observe:
      role: [accessRequests, accessGrants]
      method: POST
      json:
        - pointer: /inbox
          exists: true
    expect:
      json:
        - pointer: /inbox
          jsonType: string
          matches: "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:"
    guidance: >-
      Set "inbox" to the URL where the agent wants to hear about the request or grant.

  - id: "#client-delete-conditional"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-delete-conditional
    label: The client makes a DELETE conditional on the ETag it last read
    comment: >-
      A permission, so the outcome is information: it says whether the client uses it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#delete-resource
    traits: [Delete, Conditional]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/delete-if-match-optional
    observe:
      role: [dataResource, container]
      method: DELETE
    expect:
      otherHeaders:
        - headerName: If-Match
          present: true
    guidance: >-
      Sending If-Match with the ETag of your last read stops a delete of something that
      changed since you looked at it.

  # ---- rules that need a task (format 0.9.0): the developer's word, or a fault ----

  - id: "#client-create-container-type-link"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-create-container-type-link
    label: When the client creates a container, its POST carries Link rel="type" to lws#Container
    comment: >-
      A POST without the link creates a data resource, which is legal unless a container was
      meant, so the rule needs the developer's word: it judges the first POST into a container
      after its task starts.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#create-resource
    traits: [Post, Container]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/create-container-type-link
    task:
      prompt: Create a container, in any container you like.
    observe:
      method: POST
      role: container
    expect:
      linkHeaders:
        - rel: type
          href: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#Container
    guidance: >-
      Send Link: <https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#Container>; rel="type" with the POST. Without it,
      the server creates a data resource.

  - id: "#client-delete-container-depth"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-delete-container-depth
    label: When the client deletes a container with everything in it, it sends Depth infinity, or deletes the members first
    comment: >-
      A DELETE without Depth asks for the container alone, which is how a client deletes a
      container only if it is empty, so the rule needs the developer's word: it judges the first
      DELETE of a container after its task starts.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#delete-resource
    traits: [Delete, Container]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/delete-non-empty-container-409-depth
    task:
      prompt: Delete a container that still has something in it, together with everything in it.
    observe:
      method: DELETE
      role: container
    expect:
      anyOf:
        - otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Depth
              matches: '(?i)^\s*infinity\s*$'
        - containerEmpty: true
    guidance: >-
      Send Depth: infinity to delete a container and everything in it, or delete its members
      first. Without either, a server refuses a non-empty container with 409.

  - id: "#client-no-repeat-after-405-415"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-no-repeat-after-405-415
    label: After a linkset refuses a request with 405 or 415, the client does not send the same request again
    comment: >-
      Handling the refusal gracefully cannot be seen directly. Its visible part is that the
      client's next request to the linkset is not the refused one again: a client that reads the
      linkset's Allow and Accept-Patch, or gives up, handles it. The task makes the session
      refuse a PUT the linkset advertised, once, as a server that withdraws its optional PUT may.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Put, Patch, Linkset]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/client-no-assumed-methods-405-415
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Replace a data resource's linkset with PUT. The session will refuse the PUT once with
        405, as a server that stopped supporting it would.
      arm: methodNotAllowed
    observe:
      role: linkset
      after:
        role: linkset
        statusCode: [405, 415]
        sameTarget: true
    expect:
      repeat: false
    guidance: >-
      On a 405 or 415, read the linkset's Allow and Accept-Patch headers and change the request to
      fit them, or report the refusal. Do not send the same request again.

  - id: "#client-no-blind-retry-of-create"
    type: ObservationTest
    name: client-no-blind-retry-of-create
    label: After a create fails with a server error, the client checks before it POSTs the same thing again
    comment: >-
      When a create's answer is lost, the resource may exist. The clause allows checks or unique
      identifiers; the session cannot see an identifier a client puts in its content, so this
      rule asks that the next request to the container after a failed create is not the same
      POST again. Reading the container's listing first passes. The task makes the session
      create a resource and then answer 503.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#create-resource
    traits: [Post]
    area: core
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/create-post-not-idempotent
    task:
      prompt: >-
        Create a data resource. The session will create it and then answer 503, as if the answer
        had been lost.
      arm: lostCreateResponse
    observe:
      after:
        method: POST
        statusCode: 5xx
        sameTarget: true
    expect:
      repeat: false
    guidance: >-
      When a create fails without an answer you can trust, look at the container's listing before
      you POST again: the first POST may have worked.
